6. Authentication & Session Architecture

Authentication and authorization are separate concerns.

The platform must support secure session maintenance.

Conceptual flow:

User
→ Authentication
→ Session
→ Authorization
→ Protected resource

Requirements:

secure session handling

session expiration policy

session revocation

logout

protection against session abuse

server-side authorization

resource ownership checks

role/permission checks

The frontend must never be the authoritative source of authorization.

Unresolved decisions:

authentication provider/library

session strategy

OAuth providers, if any

email verification

password recovery

MFA requirements

session duration

refresh strategy

These must be decided through ADRs.

