9. File Upload Architecture

Large files should normally be stored in object storage rather than directly in PostgreSQL.

Database should store metadata such as:

storage key

original filename

file size

content type

checksum where appropriate

upload timestamp

ownership

submission relationship

processing status

Potential flow:

Browser
→ secure upload mechanism
→ Object Storage
→ metadata persisted in database
→ optional background processing
→ submission finalized

Security requirements:

validate file type

validate file size

validate ownership

avoid executable file exposure

use safe storage paths

do not trust filename

do not trust client-provided MIME information alone

