19. Database Design Principles

Use a relational database for transactional data.

Likely candidate:

PostgreSQL

Potential data groups:

Identity
Competition
Submission
Event
Commerce
Payment
Notification
Audit

Rules:

use foreign keys where appropriate

use unique constraints for business invariants

use transactions for atomic workflows

index based on actual query patterns

paginate large datasets

avoid N+1 queries

avoid unbounded queries

protect connection pool capacity

use migrations

never silently perform destructive migrations

ORM remains an unresolved decision.

Candidates:

Prisma

Drizzle

