44. Definition of Done

A feature is complete only if:

requirement is satisfied

architecture boundaries are preserved

authorization is correct

validation is correct

appropriate tests exist

error states exist

loading/empty states exist where relevant

responsive behavior is handled

accessibility is considered

performance impact is considered

security impact is considered

documentation is updated where required

verification has been performed

45. AI Implementation Protocol

Before implementing any major feature, the AI must provide:

Understanding

What requirement is being implemented.

Assumptions

What is known versus assumed.

Architecture Impact

Which modules, database tables, APIs, or infrastructure are affected.

Plan

Ordered implementation steps.

Risks

Security, performance, reliability, UX, and data risks.

Then implementation may begin only when no unresolved architectural blocker exists.

After implementation:

Verification

Report:

files changed

tests run

type/lint/build checks

manual verification

known limitations

